  "title": "Hyderabad: Bangladeshi girls trafficked with promises of lucrative jobs (NIA case)",
  "typology": "sex-trafficking",
  "period": "2019–2024",
  "summary": "In August 2019 Telangana police rescued five Bangladeshi girls from a house in Uppuguda, Hyderabad. India's National Investigation Agency took over the case in September 2019 and found that the accused lured Bangladeshi girls with promises of lucrative jobs and decent pay, trafficked them into India and forced them into prostitution. On 6 November 2024 the Special NIA Court in Hyderabad convicted all six accused under the Indian Penal Code and the Immoral Traffic (Prevention) Act and sentenced each to life imprisonment and a fine of Rs 24,000.",
